  "guideSudokuS1Badge": "1. CORE RULE",
  "guideSudokuS1Title": "Fill 1–9 Without Duplicates",
  "guideSudokuS1Desc": "A 9×9 Sudoku board is divided into nine 3×3 boxes. Fill every empty cell with a digit from 1 to 9.",
  "guideSudokuS1Bullets": "Every horizontal ROW must contain 1–9 with no repeats.\nEvery vertical COLUMN must contain 1–9 with no repeats.\nEvery bold 3×3 BOX must contain 1–9 with no repeats.",
  "guideSudokuS1VisualCaption": "Only 5 is missing in the center box!",
  "guideSudokuS2Badge": "2. HOW TO PLAY",
  "guideSudokuS2Title": "Tap a Cell & Use Number Highlights",
  "guideSudokuS2Desc": "Tapping any digit highlights all identical numbers across the board so you can quickly cross-check rows and columns.",
  "guideSudokuS2Bullets": "Select an empty cell, then tap 1–9 on the bottom keypad.\nOn Levels 1–4, correct placements lock automatically.\nTap the selected cell again to clear the highlight.",
  "guideSudokuS3Badge": "3. SAFE STRATEGY",
  "guideSudokuS3Title": "Use Pencil Notes & Smart Notes",
  "guideSudokuS3Desc": "Unsure between two numbers? Never guess blindly! Toggle Notes (✏️) to jot down mini candidate digits inside a cell.",
  "guideSudokuS3Bullets": "Entering Notes never costs a life (♥).\nSmart Notes automatically prunes impossible candidates.\nUse Erase to clear a cell or its pencil marks.",
  "guideSudokuS3VisualBadge": "Notes ON (Safe)",
  "guideSudokuS4Badge": "4. LIVES & ASSISTS",
  "guideSudokuS4Title": "3 Lives (♥), 3 Hints & ⚡ Auto-Finish",
  "guideSudokuS4Desc": "You start with 3 lives and up to 3 Hints. When only a few empty cells remain, the lightning Auto-Finish button appears!",
  "guideSudokuS4Bullets": "Mistakes flash red and cost 1 heart (♥).\n⚡ Auto-Finish completes the board when ≤ 5–7 cells remain.\nIn Practice Mode, Undo and Rewind on Loss are freely available!",
  "guideSudokuS4VisualBadge": "Auto-Finish (≤ 5 Left)",

  "guideMineS1Badge": "1. NUMBER MEANING",
  "guideMineS1Title": "Numbers Show Adjacent Mines",
  "guideMineS1Desc": "Every revealed number (1, 2, 3...) tells you exactly how many mines hide in the 8 surrounding tiles (including diagonals).",
  "guideMineS1Bullets": "Your first tap is ALWAYS 100% safe and opens a clear zone.\nA \"1\" means exactly 1 touching hidden tile contains a mine.\nBlank tiles (0) flood-fill open all safe neighbors automatically.",
  "guideMineS1VisualCaption": "The center \"1\" touches exactly 1 mine in the top-right corner!",
  "guideMineS2Badge": "2. DIG VS FLAG",
  "guideMineS2Title": "Plant Flags (🚩) on Suspected Mines",
  "guideMineS2Desc": "Never dig a tile you suspect is a mine! Mark it with a Flag (🚩) so it cannot be accidentally tapped.",
  "guideMineS2Bullets": "Long-press any hidden tile to place or remove a Flag.\nOr toggle the 1-Tap Swap button between Dig ⛏️ and Flag 🚩.\nYou win as soon as all safe non-mine tiles are revealed!",
  "guideMineS2VisualCaption": "Lock suspected mine tiles with a Flag (🚩)!",
  "guideMineS3Badge": "3. PRO TECHNIQUE",
  "guideMineS3Title": "Chording: Fast-Open Safe Neighbors",
  "guideMineS3Desc": "When an open number already touches the matching number of Flags (🚩), tap the number itself to open all remaining neighbors instantly!",
  "guideMineS3Bullets": "Example: A \"1\" already touches 1 Flag → tap that \"1\"!\nAll other hidden tiles touching that \"1\" open at once.\nMake sure your flag placement is accurate before chording!",
  "guideMineS4Badge": "4. BEGINNER SHIELD",
  "guideMineS4Title": "Defuse Shield (🛡️) Saves You",
  "guideMineS4Desc": "On Beginner Levels 1–2, you start with a Defuse Shield (🛡️) that automatically disarms a mine if you make a mistake!",
  "guideMineS4Bullets": "Defused mines appear safely disarmed on the board.\nPost-game review highlights all mines and any misplaced flags.\nTap View Board after a match to inspect the full mine layout.",
  "guideMineS4VisualCaption": "Lv. 1–2 Shield automatically defuses a mine!",

  "guideChessS1Badge": "1. PIECE MOVEMENTS",
  "guideChessS1Title": "How All 6 Chess Pieces Move",
  "guideChessS1Desc": "Tap any of your pieces to see legal target dots on the board. Only the Knight (♘) can jump over other pieces!",
  "guideChessS1Bullets": "♔ King: 1 step any way • ♕ Queen: any distance straight or diagonal.\n♖ Rook: straight lines • ♗ Bishop: diagonals only.\n♘ Knight: L-shape jump (2+1) • ♙ Pawn: moves forward, captures diagonally.",
  "guideChessS2Badge": "2. CHECKMATE VS STALEMATE",
  "guideChessS2Title": "Watch Out: Stalemate Is a Draw!",
  "guideChessS2Desc": "Trapping the enemy King without putting it in Check leaves them with zero legal moves—resulting in a STALEMATE (Draw), not a win!",
  "guideChessS2Bullets": "Check: King is under attack and must escape immediately.\nCheckmate: King is in Check with no legal escape → YOU WIN!\nDraw: Stalemate, 3-fold repetition, 50-move rule, or insufficient material.",
  "guideChessS2Checkmate": "CHECKMATE (Win)",
  "guideChessS2Stalemate": "STALEMATE (Draw!)",
  "guideChessS3Badge": "3. SPECIAL RULE #1",
  "guideChessS3Title": "Castling (♔⇄♖): King + Rook Double Move",
  "guideChessS3Desc": "The only move where two pieces move at once! Move your King 2 squares toward your Rook, and the Rook jumps over to the other side.",
  "guideChessS3Bullets": "Rule 1: Neither the King nor that Rook has moved yet.\nRule 2: Every square between King and Rook must be empty.\nRule 3: The King cannot be in Check or pass through an attacked square.",
  "guideChessS3VisualCaption": "Kingside Castling: King e1 → g1, Rook h1 → f1 jumps over!",
  "guideChessS4Badge": "4. SPECIAL RULE #2",
  "guideChessS4Title": "En Passant & Pawn Promotion (♙ → ♕)",
  "guideChessS4Desc": "Two crucial pawn rules that often surprise players: capturing \"in passing\" (En Passant) and promoting at the 8th rank!",
  "guideChessS4Bullets": "En Passant: When an enemy pawn advances 2 squares beside yours, you can capture it diagonally on the very next turn as if it moved 1 square.\nPromotion: Reaching the last rank transforms your pawn into a Queen (♕), Rook, Bishop, or Knight!",
  "guideChessS4VisualPromo": "Promotion → Queen",
  "guideChessS5Badge": "5. ZETZY CHESS FEATURES",
  "guideChessS5Title": "Touch Confirmation, Board Flip & Review",
  "guideChessS5Desc": "Zetzy includes thoughtful touch safeguards and post-match analysis tools.",
  "guideChessS5Bullets": "Touch Move Confirmation previews your move before locking it in.\n4 Modes: Vs AI (Lv. 1–7), Pass & Play (2P), Friend Room, & Rated Matchmaking.\nUse the post-game move scrubber (⏮ ◀ ▶ ⏭) to replay every turn!",

  "guideSnakeS1Badge": "1. CONTROLS & MOVEMENT",
  "guideSnakeS1Title": "Turn 90° & Never Bite Your Own Tail",
  "guideSnakeS1Desc": "Your snake advances smoothly across the grid. Steer toward apples while avoiding walls and your own growing body.",
  "guideSnakeS1Bullets": "Choose Swipe, Virtual D-Pad, or Split-Screen Tap in Profile settings.\nYou can turn 90° perpendicular to your heading, never 180° backward.\nArrow keys and WASD are also supported on keyboard devices.",
  "guideSnakeS2Badge": "2. APPLES & POWER-UPS",
  "guideSnakeS2Title": "Red Apples, Golden Bonus, Scissors & Poison",
  "guideSnakeS2Desc": "Learn what each arena item does to maximize your score and manage tail length!",
  "guideSnakeS2Bullets": "🍎 Red Apple (+10 pts): core food needed to reach the level target.\n🌟 Golden Apple (+30 pts): timed bonus item for massive points!\n✂️ Scissors: trims your tail shorter to free up space on the board.\n☠️ Poison: avoid! Stepping on poison triggers a hazard penalty.",
  "guideSnakeS2Trim": "Trim",
  "guideSnakeS2Hazard": "Hazard",
  "guideSnakeS3Badge": "3. WALLS & OBSTACLES",
  "guideSnakeS3Title": "Brick Walls & Dynamic Obstacles",
  "guideSnakeS3Desc": "Higher difficulty tiers introduce brick wall obstacles inside the arena that require sharp turns.",
  "guideSnakeS3Bullets": "2-Step Input Queue lets you buffer quick zig-zag turns cleanly.\nEnable Assist Overlay in settings for helpful hazard indicators.",
  "guideSnakeS3VisualCaption": "Dodge brick walls inside the arena!",
  "guideSnakeS4Badge": "4. STARVATION BAR",
  "guideSnakeS4Title": "Watch the Starvation Bar on High Tiers!",
  "guideSnakeS4Desc": "On Levels 6–7, a Starvation Bar drains over time. Eat apples promptly to refill your stamina before it runs out!",
  "guideSnakeS4Bullets": "Plan the shortest path toward the next Red Apple.\nIn Practice Mode, use Rewind 1–3 steps to recover from any crash!",
  "guideSnakeS4VisualCaption": "Starvation Timer (Lv. 6–7)",

