  "tutSudokuS1Title": "Step 1/3: Select a Cell, Then Press a Digit",
  "tutSudokuS1Exp": "The highlighted center 3×3 box already holds 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9 — only 5 is missing! To fill in Sudoku: tap the cell first, then press a digit on the number pad below.",
  "tutSudokuS1A1": "Tap the blinking empty cell in the middle of the board.",
  "tutSudokuS1A2": "Great! Now press 5 on the number pad below.",
  "tutSudokuS2Title": "Step 2/3: Pencil Candidates with Notes (✏️)",
  "tutSudokuS2Exp": "The highlighted top row is missing 3 and 4. Not sure which goes where? Don’t guess! Turn on Notes to jot small candidates — notes never cost a heart ♥.",
  "tutSudokuS2A1": "Press the blinking Notes button.",
  "tutSudokuS2A2": "Tap the first empty cell in the top row.",
  "tutSudokuS2A3": "Press 3 to note the first candidate.",
  "tutSudokuS2A4": "Press 4 to note the second candidate.",
  "tutSudokuS3Title": "Step 3/3: Eliminate & Finish!",
  "tutSudokuS3Exp": "Check that cell's column (highlighted): a 4 already sits at the bottom (yellow). Columns can't repeat, so the 3·4 cell must be 3 and its neighbor must be 4! Turn Notes off first so digits are placed for real.",
  "tutSudokuS3A1": "Turn Notes off first.",
  "tutSudokuS3A2": "Tap the cell holding the 3·4 notes.",
  "tutSudokuS3A3": "Press 3.",
  "tutSudokuS3A4": "One empty cell left beside it. Tap it.",
  "tutSudokuS3A5": "Press 4 to complete the board!",
