  "tutSudokuWrongPressDigit": "The cell is selected — now press the blinking digit below.",

  "tutMineS1Title": "Step 1/5: The First Dig Is Always Safe",
  "tutMineS1Exp": "Dig mode (⛏️) is active. In Zetzy your first dig is always safe and opens an empty area with clue numbers. A number = how many mines touch that tile (all 8 neighbors).",
  "tutMineS1A1": "Tap the blinking center tile to dig.",
  "tutMineS2Title": "Step 2/5: Plant a Flag (🚩)",
  "tutMineS2Exp": "Look at the highlighted 1 in the top row. Only ONE of its neighbors is still hidden — so that tile MUST be a mine. Switch to Flag mode, then mark it.",
  "tutMineS2A1": "Press the blinking Flag button.",
  "tutMineS2A2": "Tap the hidden tile next to the 1 to plant a Flag.",
  "tutMineS3Title": "Step 3/5: Unsure? Mark It with (?)",
  "tutMineS3Exp": "The highlighted 2 needs 2 mines. One is flagged, so the other hides in one of the 2 corner tiles. Not sure which? Use the (?) tool as a reminder — (?) tiles can’t be dug by accident.",
  "tutMineS3A1": "Press the blinking (?) button.",
  "tutMineS3A2": "Tap the top-left corner tile to mark it (?).",
  "tutMineS4Title": "Step 4/5: Find the Second Mine",
  "tutMineS4Exp": "Now check the highlighted 1 in the left column. Only one neighbor is hidden — the tile above it. That’s the second mine! Switch back to Flag.",
  "tutMineS4A1": "Press the Flag button.",
  "tutMineS4A2": "Tap the tile above that 1 to plant a Flag.",
  "tutMineS5Title": "Step 5/5: Dig the Last Safe Tile!",
  "tutMineS5Exp": "The highlighted 2 now touches 2 flags — its mine count is complete. So the (?) corner is 100% SAFE. Switch back to Dig and open it to win!",
  "tutMineS5A1": "Press the Dig button.",
  "tutMineS5A2": "Tap the (?) tile in the top-left corner to dig it.",
  "tutMineWrongSwitchTool": "Switch tools first using the blinking button below.",

  "tutChessS1Title": "Step 1/4: The Knight (♘) Jumps in an L",
  "tutChessS1Exp": "In chess, tap your piece first to see where it can go. Dots = empty squares it can reach, RED = an enemy piece it can capture. The Knight moves in an L shape and can jump over pieces.",
  "tutChessS1A1": "Tap the blinking white Knight.",
  "tutChessS1A2": "See every highlighted Knight move. The RED square holds the enemy Queen — tap it to capture!",
  "tutChessS2Title": "Step 2/4: Castling (♔⇄♖)",
  "tutChessS2Exp": "Castling = the King slides 2 squares toward a Rook, and the Rook hops to its other side. Rules: neither piece has moved, the squares between are empty, and the King is not in or passing through check.",
  "tutChessS2A1": "Tap the blinking white King first.",
  "tutChessS2A2": "The ⇄ square is the castling move. Tap it to castle!",
